From 8269983d384e4e555ae4f91c8575c0c8f417308a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Hsieh <mike_hsieh@quantatw.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:56:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] nvidia-gpu: add State.Leak.Detector support for SMA
 sensors
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This commit enhances the Nvidia SMA leak sensor to support the standard
OpenBMC Leak Detector interface and systemd target integration.

As defined in the Liquid Leak Detector design doc [1] and the existing
implementation in `src/leakdetector` [2], we start the specific systemd
target xyz.openbmc_project.leakdetector.<level>.<action>@<name>.service
upon leak state changes. This decoupled design allows platform-specific
unit files to execute necessary actions (such as emergency power-off
or alarms) without hardcoding the logic in the sensor daemon.

[1] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/73152
[2] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/75329

Tested: Build an image for sanmiguel platform.

